   $q$The narrator says the windmill "said nothing" and "kept turning its long arms." How does this description present the windmill?$q$, $q$[{"text":"As jealous, because the vane gets to sit up on the barn","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"As rude, because it will not answer the vane's questions","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"As broken, because it cannot speak like the vane can","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"As quiet and hardworking, the opposite of the bragging vane","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As quiet and hardworking, the opposite of the bragging vane$q$, $q$The narrator shows the windmill silently grinding corn while the vane brags, so the two are set up as opposites. The vane never asks a question, so the windmill is not being rude by staying quiet.$q$, 'draft', 'd5a9b747-cc36-555e-a2af-7a2d9f362593')
