-- Passage rg5-literary-structure-pov-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f3482401-1d06-52a3-bee6-7d39d4414a12', 'rg5-literary-structure-pov-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Two Sides of the Board$q$, $q$PRIYA

My hands were shaking when I sat down across from Daniel. He had won the city chess tournament last year, and everyone said he never made mistakes. He stared at the board without blinking, like a hawk. I was sure he could already see how he would beat me. When I moved my knight, he frowned. I thought he was annoyed that I was taking so long. After forty minutes, I offered a draw, and he agreed. I walked away feeling like I had escaped from a lion.

DANIEL

The girl across from me seemed so calm. She sat very still and took her time with every move. I kept staring at the board because I had no idea what to do. My stomach hurt. When she moved her knight, I frowned because I had completely missed that move. I spent the rest of the game just trying not to lose. When she offered a draw, I said yes as fast as I could. Later, I asked my coach who she was. I wanted to know how she stayed so calm.$q$, 'draft')
