   $q$What is the main effect of telling this story from two points of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that Priya was right to be afraid of Daniel all along.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that Daniel is a much better chess player than Priya.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains the rules of chess from a beginner's and an expert's view.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It shows that each player misread the other, since both were nervous.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that each player misread the other, since both were nervous.$q$, $q$Priya thinks Daniel is fearless, and Daniel thinks Priya is calm, but each section shows the speaker was worried, so readers see what neither player could. Daniel's section shows he was struggling, so Priya's fear of him was not proven right.$q$, 'draft', 'f3482401-1d06-52a3-bee6-7d39d4414a12')
