   $q$Because the bus is the speaker, how are the riders described?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Through their private thoughts about their own lives","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-with-character"},{"text":"As people the bus watches come and go along its route","is_correct":true},{"text":"As strangers the bus does not notice at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Through a long conversation between the riders","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$As people the bus watches come and go along its route$q$, $q$The bus notices outside details, like a baker "dusted white with flour" and backpacks bumping, as riders get on and off. A bus cannot know their private thoughts, and the poem never shares them.$q$, 'draft', '1189a38b-da30-5eac-bcdf-dc53c9245399')
