   $q$Why is it important that Chapter 1 shows Rosa practicing every evening?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains how Rosa is able to understand the warning in Chapter 2.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains why Aunt Marisol leaves Rosa alone during storms.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It shows that the telegraph machine was broken most of the time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that Rosa wants to become a train driver someday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains how Rosa is able to understand the warning in Chapter 2.$q$, $q$Because Rosa practiced until clicks "turned into letters in her head," she can decode "Bridge. Out. Cedar Creek." when she is alone. Aunt Marisol leaves to help a neighbor, not because Rosa practiced.$q$, 'draft', '189b3fb7-c10b-59e6-b29c-4d02a18c8b07')
