   $q$The narrator says the truck "rumbled like an angry dog." What does this comparison show about the narrator's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The truck driver was angry about carrying boxes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The narrator is excited to ride inside the truck.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The family brought a dog with them on the truck.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To a cat, the loud truck seems unfriendly and scary.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To a cat, the loud truck seems unfriendly and scary.$q$, $q$A cat would see an angry dog as a threat, so the comparison shows how frightening the truck seems to Biscuit. There is no real dog in the story; the dog is only a comparison.$q$, 'draft', '2aec90ce-8690-57bb-9f35-95af48f2911e')
